you open windows wider than your physical screen
(_not_ MS-Windows, but many Linux/Unix
GUI implementations do), just adjust the window to
non-full screen, grab the title bar, slide the window
nearly full left, widen it nearly full right, grab the title
bar again and slide the window right to put the
unwanted ad bar off-screen, retaining the rest of the
screen for useful work. You'll need to slide the
window left again to access the few tools on the
right edge, but you hardly ever use those, so, so
what.

